{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Remediation update after change 2962 merged: manual Windows run 34466319475 showed the original fcntl collection failure was gone and the named Windows exclusive-leg proof step passed, but the continue-on-error Windows default suite exposed a follow-on topology-copy setup failure in tests/_topology_template.py. Local root cause: helpers used git -C against copied bare remotes, which fails under safe.bareRepository=explicit and can skip sibling remote rewrites; Windows paths may also be slash-normalized in Git config. Expanded file impact accordingly. Targeted validation now passes: 33 passed, 2 skipped for the fcntl guard modules plus tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_copy_repoints_sibling_origin_and_keeps_refs_isolated. Full make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2 lint/typecheck passed and pytest progressed past 50%, but I stopped it after ~82 minutes to avoid missing the cutoff; the observed active tests pass individually."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789046801369608001,"uuid":"a72dc250-6724-43a9-8567-37ba1e43f6d5"}